{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1488996-some-questions-about-vitae-posthumous-embraces-and-revenants","id":1488996,"title":"Some questions about Vitae, Posthumous Embraces and Revenants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-03T11:45:10-07:00","id":1488996,"title":"Some questions about Vitae, Posthumous Embraces and Revenants","content":"I\u2019ve been reading through the 2nd Edition of <b>Vampire: The Requiem </b>and noticed that I struggle to understand some of the important points in the \u201cthe life-cycle\u201d of the Kindred, Ghouls and Revenants. As this is my first time reading anything <b>WoD</b> related, the questions pondered in this post are likely to be seen as trivial by the veterans of this community. Still, I thought the post is in order xD <hr />So, it is mentioned that a typical <b>Embrace </b>is accomplished by first draining a person of blood, killing them in the process, and then feeding point of vampire\u2019s <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vitae </b></span>to their still-warm body. The same Vitae, though, will react differently to being fed to a living person \u2014 it will not Embrace them, but make them into a Ghoul instead (at least until Vitae\u2019s effects wear off, after which a person supposedly becomes a simple mortal). Also, in both cases the kindred sharing their Vitae will risk the Blood Bond being formed.<br /> <br /> I would assume that <b>Posthumous Embraces</b> happen when dead bodies come into close contact with Vitae, but not immediately after their death. As this form of Embrace produces the same results as the traditional ritual, I can only conclude a simple contact of a dead body and vampire\u2019s Vitae is enough to create a full-fledged kindred. (Isn\u2019t every Embrace \u201cPosthumous\u201d? Cause the person needs to die before being fed Vitae)<br /> <br /> So-far it seems to be logical. We\u2019ve got this set of rules: <span style=\"color:#008000\">Alive Body</span> + <span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vitae</span> = Ghoul, <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Dead Body</span> + <span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vitae </span>= Kindred (both for typical and posthumous embraces).<br /> So, how do <b>Revenants </b>fit into this picture?<br /> <br /> They are described as <i>\u201clesser vampires that sometimes rise from those contaminated by the <b>Kindred bite</b> or <b>Kindred blood</b>, as well as from <b>victims of violent feedings</b> and dead <b>Ghouls</b>\u201d.</i> Also it is mentioned that: <i>\u201ckindred that are aware of the possibility of revenants often destroy the corpses of the dead in ways that prevent them from rising as vampires, while some feed with needles and other tools to avoid contaminating their victims\u201d</i><br /> <br /> So, the people that are contaminated by <b>Kindred\u2019s blood</b> (Vitae) have the chance of rising as Revenants. That, based on the writing, includes Ghouls that still have Vitae circulating through their veins. But we have already established that Vitae + Dead Bodies result in Kindred. Why wouldn\u2019t those Ghouls, if Vitae in their veins can indeed bring them back to life, just rise as Vampires? Or is it the fact the Vitae was administered to them <b>before</b> their death, not after, that makes them into Revenants? And how do victims of violent feeding come into this picture? They have never been given Vitae, either before or after death.<br /> <br /> Also, what does it mean to be contaminated by <b>\u201cKindred bite\u201d</b>? I understand the concept of Vitae contamination, but how does Vampires feeding on someone contaminate the people? Is it Kindred saliva during the Kiss that contaminates the mortals? Is it purely supernatural \u201cmark\u201d that is imprinted upon those whose blood Vampires drank?<br /> <br /> For Caine's sake, what are the answers?! xD<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27533-vargock","name":"Vargock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T12:04:33-07:00","id":1488997,"title":"","content":"The vampiric condition is a Curse, and follows sympathetic, magical logic about as much as it does predictable causation. Contamination does not have a consistent physical factor. If you've been bitten, you've been contaminated by the bite. Kindred carry a subtle intrinsic taint.<br /> <br /> The subject of a posthumous Embrace must be someone who has been fed Vitae at some point in the past. (They need not have been ghouled; ghouling requires not just a draught of Vitae but a conscious investment of will by the vampire.) A lingering taint makes the body receptive without fresh exsanguination. Simply dripping Vitae into the mouth of any dead body doesn't suffice. Simply having Vitae in your system at the moment of death also doesn't suffice for a full posthumous Embrace. You need the unnatural resurrection of receiving Vitae after the point of death. Vitae is stolen life. The undead rise from life in death.<br /> <br /> Revenants are a subsidiary Curse and a sympathetic consequence of the corruption wrought by the Kindred.<br /> <br /> The Kindred condition is a Curse. The Curse is bad and it makes bad things happen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}